    {
      "type": "note",
      "id": "c78Nt",
      "x": 1040,
      "y": 40,
      "name": "378 notes",
      "width": 620,
      "height": 0,
      "content": "Feature 378 / impl 0042 — mission channel composer\n\n• The composer is the HUMAN side of the already-shipped channel: runners broadcast with `runner msg post` today; this posts kind=message from=\"human\" (to=null broadcast, to=@handle targeted). No new signals or routing.\n• Pinned under the feed, top hairline aligned with the app's divider language. Primary window only (secondary stays read-only).\n• Typing @ at position 0 opens the roster picker above the box (third frame): handle + slot role · runtime per row, ↑↓ to move, ↵/Tab selects → accent chip, Esc dismisses; typing filters the list. Only a leading @ targets — mid-text @ never opens the picker and stays plain broadcast text. Unknown @word falls through as typed.\n• Enter sends, Shift+Enter newline. No send button — terminal-flavored surface; the ↵ hint sits inside the box (drop if it reads as noise, cf. the esc keycap removal in 56).\n• Human rows: author \"you\" in amber ($warn) — runner handles keep accent green; targeted rows show \"→ @handle\". Matches the ask-card's human-interaction amber.\n• Delivery: nudges land at turn boundaries via existing message_nudge; the feed row appears immediately."
    },
